cc-mod-academic-harness
=======================

A Claude Code mod that runs the Academic Harness research tooling inside Claude
Code. It is a port, not a fork: the upstream project is read at a pinned commit
(UPSTREAM.lock.json) and never modified.

Code written for this mod (hooks/, server/, scripts/, tests/, types/, docs/, the
generated agents/ and the build tooling) is under the MIT License in LICENSE.

Upstream
--------

Academic Harness, MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 ResearchCraft,
https://github.com/raktim-mondol/academic-harness.

Its tool modules, writing engine, PaperMemory and prompt are NOT in this
repository. The plugin downloads the pinned commit on first start into the
mod's home folder and checks it against the digests in UPSTREAM.lock.json. That
download is upstream's own distribution and carries upstream's NOTICE, which
lists every third-party skill catalogue it bundles and each one's licence. Some
of those skills are licensed for non-commercial use only (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0), and
some name a GPL library; they remain under their own licences, and this mod's
MIT licence does not relicense them. A skill's `license:` line in its frontmatter
names the licence it is under. None of them is copied into this repository (see
below), but a skill the model fetches on demand from the downloaded snapshot may
be one of them: read its `license:` line before reusing its text.

What is copied into this repository
-----------------------------------

skills/ and agents/ are generated from the snapshot by scripts/build-skills.mjs
and scripts/build-agents.mjs. The build leaves out every skill whose licence is
non-commercial, GPL or unknown (decision D5), and records what it copied and
what it left out, with each licence, in skills/.build-info.json. Of the 54
skills copied, 36 name MIT, 3 name CC-BY-4.0, and 15 name no licence because
they are the source's own text. Most are first-party Academic Harness skills
(MIT). The ones that come from other projects, and what each needs, are:

